From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] buttonmatrix: draw button texts as static text

Button texts were copied into each draw task (text_local), so the OpenGL ES
draw unit could not cache them: it rendered every key of a keyboard on the
CPU and uploaded it again on every frame. The map has to stay valid while it
is used, so draw from it directly as static text (except with Arabic/Persian
processing, which writes the text into a local buffer).
---
--- a/src/widgets/buttonmatrix/lv_buttonmatrix.c
+++ b/src/widgets/buttonmatrix/lv_buttonmatrix.c
@@ -812,7 +812,13 @@
 
         /*Draw the text*/
         draw_label_dsc_act.text = txt;
+#if LV_USE_ARABIC_PERSIAN_CHARS
         draw_label_dsc_act.text_local = true;
+#else
+        /*The map has to stay valid: draw the text from it, as static text that GPU
+         *draw units can cache (they render and upload other text on every frame)*/
+        draw_label_dsc_act.text_static = true;
+#endif
         draw_label_dsc_act.base.id1 = btn_i;
         lv_draw_label(layer, &draw_label_dsc_act, &btn_area);
     }
